BIOT receives windows whose channels are each divided by the 95th percentile of their absolute value, as in its authors' pretraining and downstream loaders (`utils.py` of their repository). The backend applies it to the 16 bipolar channels, for embeddings and for fine-tuning; `FoundationModelSpec.input_normalization` names the normalisation and is recorded with the embeddings. BIOT was fed plain microvolts before, so its embeddings and fine-tunes change and must be recomputed.
